-- Migration 110 (up): a garbled-text repair is offered, never applied unasked (the 3.18.0 release audit: the repair cannot tell damage from an author's own example, and johal.in's guide to mojibake quotes such text on purpose). text_repair_offer names each post with text that can be restored: state 'offered' is listed on the Posts page to review; 'kept' is the author's "keep as written", remembered with a fingerprint (sig) of the runs it was given for, so the same text is not offered again but different text is. NOTE: runMigrations executes line-by-line, so keep each statement on ONE line.
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS text_repair_offer(slug TEXT PRIMARY KEY, runs INTEGER NOT NULL, sig TEXT NOT NULL, state TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'offered' CHECK(state IN ('offered','kept')), found_at DATETIME NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP);
